+# Challenger panel corrections ? 14 November 2026
+
+The owner's four marked defects are corrected in the native model: the rear uses one symmetric continuous loft, the door bottom has a rounded fitted contour and regular skin, the grille surround has a rolled upper bridge and clean lower edge, and the bonnet has a smooth analytic boundary and surface. This replaces the previous pass's inadequate appearance acceptance. Owner review after restarting the game and physical-device qualification remain separate.
+
+| Requirement | Change |
+|---|---|
+| CPC01 | Replace disconnected lower rear patches with one loft around both quarters and bumper. Mirror final packed geometry and normal splits; seat taillights, lower reflectors and side markers on the corrected skins. |
+| CPC02 | Fillet the lower door corners, fit narrow paired contour ribbons and replace the long interpolation triangles in the lower door. |
+| CPC03 | Share the nose bridge and rolled return, close its ends, and trim the lower grille aperture after reduction. |
+| CPC04 | Author the bonnet directly in final car coordinates, with rounded corners, a bounded smooth crown and three clean vent apertures. Bake its narrow inset marking and lower edge return offline. |
+| CPC05 | Keep repaired compact skins immutable through generic production reduction; retain that reduction for the remaining parts. Refresh derived resources and keep the existing 50k/85k uncoarsened allocation and canonical handling/contact controls. |
+
+The authored sources are `scripts/challenger_clean_panels.py`, `scripts/prepare_challenger.py`, `game/tests/bake_challenger_hellcat.gd`, `game/vehicle/challenger_panel_contours.gd` and the metadata guard in `game/vehicle/car_mesh_lods.gd`. `game/tests/test_panel_contours.gd` validates the new native-marking contract while retaining its original 100-segment runtime-fallback checks. Native assets, the new coarse recipes and dependent prepared/presentation resources are regenerated; no handling source or car configuration is authored.
+
+The bonnet marking now bypasses the old two triangle-mesh constructions and per-edge ray fitting during procedural construction. It remains in the same contour/material batch. Both tiers retain 22 native material batches and use no cabin geometry or transparent windows. Valid prepared cars already bypass procedural construction; no loading-time improvement or physical-device performance is claimed from this correction.
+
+The repair deliberately spends more geometry on coherent surfaces than the previous defective simplification. With further coarse reduction disabled, the assembled reduced/full cars are **49,808 / 83,936 triangles**, below the unchanged **50,000 / 85,000** allocations. The normal reduced stock model is **39,368 triangles**, for both fixed and editable construction. The preceding production stock was 25,918, while its uncoarsened constructors were 45,150 / 77,204. The increased cost protects the owner's requested appearance; this is not a further triangle-saving claim.
+
+[Compatibility before/after](evidence/challenger-panel-corrections-2026-11-14/comparison-gl_compatibility.png) and [Vulkan Mobile before/after](evidence/challenger-panel-corrections-2026-11-14/comparison-mobile.png) compare the four marked views. [Full-resolution prepared views](evidence/challenger-panel-corrections-2026-11-14/prepared/) retain both detail tiers and red-paint reflection angles. [Actual App captures](evidence/challenger-panel-corrections-2026-11-14/app/) cover Garage and a local race.
+
+The native payload grows by 207,484 bytes in the reduced tier and 253,400 bytes in the full tier; material batches remain 22 in each. [Measurements](evidence/challenger-panel-corrections-2026-11-14/metrics.json) include native triangles, raw buffers and disk bytes. The automatic App readiness traces are functional smoke results, not a controlled before/after loading benchmark.
+
+The focused native fixture checks both tiers for reflected positions/normals, door continuity, smooth rear curvature, closed quarter skins, taillight and reflector visibility, grille edge accuracy, protected production boundaries, ribbon topology and supported bonnet edges. Native compressed coordinates are compared within one AABB quantisation unit plus 2 micrometres, with a one-milliradian normal tolerance. The same final fixture rejects the task-start geometry; final results and render comparisons are linked below.
+
+Native corrections were developed in private candidates. Rejected drafts included unsupported hood surrounds, excessive clipping fragments, contour pairing faults, taillight occlusion and the reduced-tier allocation overrun. None of those candidates was published. A preliminary quarter-curvature probe incorrectly treated the intended rounded turn as a dent; the final probe rejects reverse-curvature spikes, keeping a stricter 1 mm limit. Normal comparison was calibrated to the actual packed format, and the native baker now reconstructs both halves from one packed side so normal-split welding cannot introduce different shading.
+
+Publication checks exact conversion inputs, the previous live native files, all eight car configurations and the focused geometry receipt. It writes the manifest last and restores previous bytes on handled failure. The shared index is never used for the source checkpoint. The workshop is regenerated solely because its declared inputs include the shared LOD policy; no Garage prop source is authored.
+
+Final checks use Godot 4.7.2 and isolated offline profiles. Every linked command receipt records the actual executable, arguments, source pin, process result and duration; no planned run is counted as passed.
+
+| Actual command / receipt | Result |
+|---|---|
+| [`python run_preparation.py`](evidence/challenger-panel-corrections-2026-11-14/preparation-command.json), then [native bake](evidence/challenger-panel-corrections-2026-11-14/native-final-command.json) | Exact converter/art/label fences; both tiers generated; qualified triangle counts retained. |
+| [Focused native geometry, live assets](evidence/challenger-panel-corrections-2026-11-14/panels-live-command.json) | 34 checks / 0 failures; identical fixture rejects task-start geometry with 34 / 24. |
+| [Uncoarsened stock allocation / contacts](evidence/challenger-panel-corrections-2026-11-14/native-allocation-final-command.json) | 17 / 0; reduced 49,808, full 83,936 triangles. The earlier 50,498-triangle draft was rejected. |
+| [`test_panel_contours.gd`](evidence/challenger-panel-corrections-2026-11-14/contours-final-command.json) | 172 / 0; physical widths, unchanged native positions, no runtime bonnet geometry, exact provenance and supported inset markings. |
